---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Martin Tahli's approach to products, systems, engineering, and people."
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">About Martin</p>
      <h1>
        Products are systems.
        <br />
        People are part of them.
      </h1>
      <p class="lede">{profile.background}</p>
    </header>
    <section class="section split">
      <h2>An engineering foundation.</h2>
      <div class="measure">
        <p>
          Firmware and software are the foundation of my work. My focus is the
          wider system: what needs to happen, where the boundaries belong, and
          how to know whether it behaves correctly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section split">
      <h2>
        AI as leverage.
        <br />
        Judgment stays human.
      </h2>
      <div class="measure">
        <p>
          I use AI to support architecture, implementation, and iteration. That
          does not remove the need to understand the problem, inspect the
          output, or validate the result.
        </p>
        <p>
          For this portfolio, the product and design specifications come first.
          Changes are reviewed against those constraints, and unverified checks
          stay visible rather than being treated as passes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section split">
      <h2>How I make decisions.</h2>
      <ol class="principles">
        <li>Understand the problem before choosing the implementation.</li>
        <li>Use automation to buy back thinking time.</li>
        <li>Treat UX as system behavior, not decoration.</li>
        <li>Test uncertain assumptions cheaply.</li>
        <li>Make tradeoffs explicit.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section class="section split">
      <h2>The useful question.</h2>
      <div class="measure">
        <p>
          Not just “does it run?” but “does the whole system help someone do
          what they need to do?” Architecture and the experience of using a
          product need to answer that question together.
        </p>
        <a
          class="text-link"
          href={withBase('/work/', import.meta.env.BASE_URL)}
        >
          Explore the work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .principles {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }
  .principles li {
    padding: 0 0 1.25rem 0.75rem;
  }
  .principles li::marker {
    color: var(--text-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }
</style>
